From: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:05:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Do not warn on RWX LOAD segments

Binutils 2.39 warns when a segment has RWX permissions, and this tree
links with --fatal-warnings, so bl31.elf fails to link:

  ld.bfd: warning: build/lx2160acex7/release/bl31/bl31.elf has a LOAD
  segment with RWX permissions

The segment layout is what it has always been; only the linker became
noisier. Suppress the warning, as upstream TF-A did in review 19401 and
as meta-freescale already carries for its own qoriq-atf 2.12 recipe.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://review.trustedfirmware.org/c/TF-A/trusted-firmware-a/+/19401]

Adapted to the 1.5 Makefile, which has no ld.lld guard around the line.

Signed-off-by: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
---
 Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -175,7 +175,7 @@ endif
 
 TF_LDFLAGS		+=	--fatal-warnings -O1
 TF_LDFLAGS		+=	--gc-sections
-TF_LDFLAGS		+=	$(TF_LDFLAGS_$(ARCH))
+TF_LDFLAGS		+=	$(TF_LDFLAGS_$(ARCH)) --no-warn-rwx-segments
 
 DTC_FLAGS		+=	-I dts -O dtb
 
